# GUARD unmeasured-cell-is-null
#
# `Session.cell_width`/`cell_height` were plain floats defaulting to 8 and 18,
# and the PAINTER was their only writer -- so every reader that ran before the
# first paint got "the estimate for font-size 13" while believing it held a
# measurement. Three separate `if (cell_width <= 0 or cell_height <= 0)` guards
# had been written to catch exactly that, and not one could ever fire, because
# 8 and 18 are both positive.
#
# The break restores those defaults through the optional. Note that it is
# invisible at font-size 13: round(13*0.6) = 8 and round(13*1.4) = 18 are the
# wrong values AND the right ones. The test goes red under this break only
# because it is written at font-size 26. A test at the default font could not.
#
test: a pane proposes no viewport until its cell box has been measured
red: 2026-08-12 at 5bccbd2
diff --git a/src/terminal/session.zig b/src/terminal/session.zig
index bfb06b2..b4c0001 100644
--- a/src/terminal/session.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/session.zig
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@ pub const Session = struct {
     /// The mono face's cell box at the terminal type size, or NULL until the
     /// painter has actually measured it. See `CellBox` for why this is an
     /// optional rather than a pair of floats with plausible defaults.
-    measured_cell: ?CellBox = null,
+    measured_cell: ?CellBox = .{ .width = 8, .height = 18 },
     font_size: f32 = 13,
     /// Reused projection buffers for `snapshot` (see that function). The
     /// first-party painter takes a RESOLVED snapshot whose every slice
